{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/caller.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve.caller\n     2\t  \"Call-out readiness at the calling peer: the composition step that\n     3\t   makes a remote call pair ready for a VM before the VM is built.\n     4\t\n     5\t   A VM built over a supplied call pair needs its call-out cursor at\n     6\t   construction (`yin.vm/empty-state` refuses a supplied `:call-out`\n     7\t   without `:call-out-cursor`). Over reflections of a served endpoint\n     8\t   that cursor is a remote answer: the reflection's first `cursor`\n     9\t   answers retry while its request crosses, and only a later ask, after\n    10\t   the drive owner has moved the channel, finds the answer filed. The VM\n    11\t   must not learn that cadence -- readiness belongs to the driver, not\n    12\t   the stream -- so it lives here, in the caller's composition.\n    13\t\n    14\t   `open` attaches both reflections of an apply endpoint and checks the\n    15\t   caller token. `step` asks the call-out reflection once for a\n    16\t   `:dao.stream/newest` cursor: the cursor lands after every response\n    17\t   already on the shared stream, so this caller reads only responses to\n    18\t   requests it sends afterwards. `step` yields `::pending` on retry or\n    19\t   blocked, `::ready` with the minted cursor once it is filed, and is\n    20\t   terminal (`::refused`, `::exhausted`) otherwise; `::max-attempts`\n    21\t   bounds the asks. The drive owner steps its channel between steps.\n    22\t   `vm-opts` then answers the construction options -- the pair, the\n    23\t   cursor, and the caller token -- for any VM's `create-vm`.\n    24\t\n    25\t   The caller value is a plain value threaded by its owner; nothing here\n    26\t   loops, waits or reads a clock.\"\n    27\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n    28\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n    29\t            [yin.vm :as vm]))\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\t(def default-max-attempts\n    33\t  \"How many cursor asks `step` makes before it gives up as `::exhausted`.\"\n    34\t  16)\n    35\t\n    36\t\n    37\t(defn- refused\n    38\t  [option reason]\n    39\t  {::status ::refused, ::refusals [{::option option, ::reason reason}]})\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\t(defn- attach\n    43\t  [attach! descriptor]\n    44\t  (let [r (try (attach! descriptor)\n    45\t               (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil))]\n    46\t    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n    47\t      (:dao.stream/handle r))))\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\t(defn- portable-id?\n    51\t  \"True when the call ids this caller mints survive `codec` -- encoded,\n    52\t   decoded back. No codec asserts nothing more than plain data.\"\n    53\t  [codec caller-id]\n    54\t  (let [id [caller-id :parked-0]]\n    55\t    (or (nil? codec)\n    56\t        (try (= id ((:decode codec) ((:encode codec) id)))\n    57\t             (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ false)))))\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t(defn open\n    61\t  \"Attach the call pair of apply `::endpoint` through `::attach!` (the\n    62\t   caller's attacher, `(fn [descriptor] -> attach outcome)`), for the\n    63\t   caller tenure named by `::caller-id` -- a token the composition mints,\n    64\t   unique per tenure (`yin.vm/ffi-caller-id?`). Optional:\n    65\t   `::max-attempts` (default `default-max-attempts`), and `::codec`, the\n    66\t   channel codec `{:encode f :decode f}` the call ids must survive.\n    67\t\n    68\t   Returns the caller value, `::status ::pending`, or\n    69\t   `{::status ::refused ::refusals [...]}` before anything is attached\n    70\t   when an option is malformed, or naming the reflection that did not\n    71\t   attach.\"\n    72\t  [opts]\n    73\t  (let [{::keys [endpoint attach! caller-id max-attempts codec]} opts\n    74\t        max-attempts (or max-attempts default-max-attempts)]\n    75\t    (cond\n    76\t      (not (fn? attach!)) (refused ::attach! ::malformed)\n    77\t      (not (apply2/endpoint? endpoint)) (refused ::endpoint ::malformed)\n    78\t      (not (vm/ffi-caller-id? caller-id)) (refused ::caller-id ::malformed)\n    79\t      (not (portable-id? codec caller-id)) (refused ::caller-id ::unportable)\n    80\t      (not (and (int? max-attempts) (pos? max-attempts)))\n    81\t      (refused ::max-attempts ::malformed)\n    82\t      :else\n    83\t      (if-some [in (attach attach! (apply2/endpoint-request endpoint))]\n    84\t        (if-some [out (attach attach! (apply2/endpoint-response endpoint))]\n    85\t          {::status ::pending,\n    86\t           ::call-in in,\n    87\t           ::call-out out,\n    88\t           ::caller-id caller-id,\n    89\t           ::attempts 0,\n    90\t           ::max-attempts max-attempts}\n    91\t          (refused ::call-out ::unattached))\n    92\t        (refused ::call-in ::unattached)))))\n    93\t\n    94\t\n    95\t(defn step\n    96\t  \"Ask the call-out reflection once for a `:dao.stream/newest` cursor.\n    97\t   `ok` makes the caller `::ready` with that cursor; retry or blocked\n    98\t   leaves it `::pending`, or `::exhausted` once `::max-attempts` asks\n    99\t   have gone unanswered; any other outcome refuses it with that\n   100\t   `::outcome`. A caller that is not pending is returned unchanged.\"\n   101\t  [caller]\n   102\t  (if-not (= ::pending (::status caller))\n   103\t    caller\n   104\t    (let [r (stream/cursor (::call-out caller) stream/anchor-newest)\n   105\t          o (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   106\t          attempts (inc (::attempts caller))]\n   107\t      (cond\n   108\t        (= :dao.stream/ok o)\n   109\t        (assoc caller\n   110\t               ::status ::ready\n   111\t               ::attempts attempts\n   112\t               ::call-out-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   113\t        (or (= :dao.stream/blocked o) (:dao.stream/retry? r))\n   114\t        (assoc caller\n   115\t               ::status (if (< attempts (::max-attempts caller))\n   116\t                          ::pending\n   117\t                          ::exhausted)\n   118\t               ::attempts attempts)\n   119\t        :else (assoc caller\n   120\t                     ::status ::refused\n   121\t                     ::attempts attempts\n   122\t                     ::outcome o)))))\n   123\t\n   124\t\n   125\t(defn ready?\n   126\t  [caller]\n   127\t  (= ::ready (::status caller)))\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t(defn call-out-cursor\n   131\t  \"The minted call-out cursor of a ready caller, else nil.\"\n   132\t  [caller]\n   133\t  (when (ready? caller) (::call-out-cursor caller)))\n   134\t\n   135\t\n   136\t(defn vm-opts\n   137\t  \"The construction options a ready caller hands any VM's `create-vm`:\n   138\t   `:call-in`, `:call-out`, `:call-out-cursor` and `:ffi-caller-id`.\n   139\t   nil when the caller is not ready.\"\n   140\t  [caller]\n   141\t  (when (ready? caller)\n   142\t    {:call-in (::call-in caller),\n   143\t     :call-out (::call-out caller),\n   144\t     :call-out-cursor (::call-out-cursor caller),\n   145\t     :ffi-caller-id (::caller-id caller)}))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat collab/1790655248000-vm-engineer-ffi-caller-correlation.prompt.md; sed -n '48,65p' collab/1790654484000-architect-ffi-correlation-second-opinion.glm-5.3.findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-09-29 04:14:08 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-09-29 11:14:08 +07 (+0700)\nCoding-Agent: claude\nSession-ID: 08d36f7d-b33d-404e-adcb-dc04d5b907ef\n# Task: Slice 3d — caller-scoped FFI correlation, FFI response router, caller call-out readiness, portable loss error\n\nRole: Yin.VM Runtime Engineer\n\nImplementers:\n- Model: claude-opus-5-5 | Assigned: 2026-09-29 11:14:08 +07 (+0700) | Status: active | Rationale: owner-authorized VM correction; new session on the committed 3c base (c9313ee0)\n\nImplement Slice 3d in /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld (master c9313ee0; 3a b34643c0, 3b c2417899, 3c c9313ee0 landed).\nIMPLEMENTATION: edits authorized in the named files only. Do not stage or commit. This slice completes remote FFI.\n\nOWNER DECISIONS (verbatim selected options):\n- \"Authorize all 8 (Recommended) — Dispatch 3d implementing gpt-6-sol's ruling with glm-5.3's five changes folded in;\n  gated by gpt-6-sol with glm-5.3's findings in the gate brief.\"\n- Supplied-pair policy: \"Refuse (Recommended) — glm-5.3's recommendation: extend the half-a-pair check so a supplied\n  pair without a composition-minted cursor is refused at construction; avoids scanning a shared ring from :oldest and\n  spurious gap-loss.\"\n\nGoverning design (read in full; where they differ, glm-5.3's CHANGES amend gpt-6-sol's ruling):\n- collab/1790594862000-architect-ffi-serving-slice3-r3.gpt-6-sol.findings.md (the ruling: sections 1-4)\n- collab/1790654484000-architect-ffi-correlation-second-opinion.glm-5.3.findings.md (CONCUR WITH CHANGES; its\n  \"Changes to the ruling\" 1-5 are binding)\n- the gate finding being fixed: collab/1790611924000-reviewer-ffi-responder-e2e-gate.gpt-6-sol.findings.md (P1, P2\n  readiness, Q3)\n- collab/1790575143000-architect-one-envelope-ruling.gpt-6-sol.findings.md (the request map travels unchanged;\n  apply/correlation-id? stays some?; do not tighten apply's predicates; rpc's allocator untouched)\n- docs/design/datom.world.md invariants; docs/design/dao.stream.md (readiness belongs to the driver)\n- 3c code: src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve{.cljc,/responder.cljc,/holder.cljc}, its tests; implementer report\n  collab/1790610416000-vm-engineer-ffi-responder-e2e.claude-opus-5-5.report.md (Unresolved 1-3 are what you fix)\n- docs/agents/build-n-test.md\n\nScope (summary; the rulings are authoritative):\n1. Composite call ids [caller-token local-park-id]: the caller's host composition mints a portable unique token per VM\n   caller tenure and passes it as :ffi-caller-id at construction; the composite id is ALSO the parked-map key (one id,\n   no second mapping); engine/park-continuation takes an optional explicit id; all four FFI call sites (semantic,\n   ast_walker, debruijn/stack, debruijn/register) supply it. Token must satisfy vm/plain-data? and the channel codec.\n   Local/legacy behaviour without :ffi-caller-id must keep working (existing tests unchanged).\n2. FFI response router in yin.vm.engine beside the link poll (glm change 4): bounded per cursor cell INCLUDING carried\n   cells of lowered retained calls; advance the cell on every ok; wake only the live FFI waiter whose :call-id equals\n   apply/response-id; keep others parked; discard or diagnose responses for no live waiter; terminal read wakes the\n   affected waiters as loss; match both entry shapes (walker nests :call-id in :k); exclude FFI response entries from\n   the generic waitset sweep as link entries are; dao.stream.waitset itself unchanged. Envelope interpretation may live\n   in yin.vm.ffi with check-wait-set dispatching into it. ffi/call-result stays the final validation.\n3. debruijn_register_effects validators (~412, ~432) accept the composite id shape (glm change 1) + their tests.\n4. Readiness: a bounded, state-threaded caller-composition step (new ns under src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/, e.g.\n   remote_serve/caller.cljc) that attaches both reflections, obtains a :newest call-out cursor, yields on retry, and\n   returns the minted cursor; new trusted :call-out-cursor construction option installed by yin.vm/empty-state; local\n   pairs keep their current mint; a SUPPLIED pair without :call-out-cursor is REFUSED at construction (owner decision;\n   extend the half-a-pair check ~vm.cljc:2012). Replace the test-only pre-poll with the production step.\n5. Loss error: on FFI response-stream end, raise ex-info {:call-id id :error {:dao.stream.apply/code\n   :dao.stream.apply/ended :dao.stream.apply/message \"...\"}}; same for gap with a gap-specific message AND a\n   machine-distinguishing extra key in the error map (glm change 3; the error map is open). Replaces the generic\n   \"FFI response envelope is malformed\" for these cases.\n\nAllowed files: src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc, src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc, src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc,\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc, src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc, src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc,\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc, src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc; their existing tests;\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/** and test/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/** (+ remote_serve_test.cljc);\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc (acceptance checks only; ucf/remote.cljc itself must not change). Anything else\n(dao.stream.*, dao.lease, yin.vm.ucf.remote source, yang.*): STOP and report.\n\nAcceptance (each must fail if broken; prove the load-bearing ones by temporary mutation, revert, grep):\na. Two VMs on ONE exported pair, responses arriving in the OPPOSITE order to the requests: each VM receives its own\n   result (this is the regression test for the gate P1).\nb. A VM whose unrelated response arrives first stays parked and is woken later by its own; a response with no live\n   waiter is discarded/diagnosed, never delivered.\nc. Readiness: the production step yields on retry and returns a real cursor; VM built with it completes a remote call;\n   a supplied pair without :call-out-cursor is refused at construction.\nd. Loss: response-stream end -> portable :dao.stream.apply/ended error with the call id; gap -> same code, distinct\n   machine key; neither raises \"malformed envelope\".\ne. Migrated retained call: lift/lower a parked FFI call carrying a composite id across UCF, resume on the other host,\n   correlate correctly (carried cursor cell is routed).\nf. All four VM kinds (semantic, ast_walker, debruijn stack, debruijn register) park and resume with composite ids;\n   register effects validators accept them; a CLJD-relevant check that a vector parked key round-trips.\ng. Every existing yin.vm / ffi / ucf / remote_serve test still passes unchanged except where a test asserted the old\n   id shape or the old generic error (update those minimally and list each).\n\nPortable CLJC (CLJ/CLJS/CLJD): on CLJD #?(:clj ...) is NOT excluded — use #?(:cljd nil :clj ...) with :cljd first;\nno cross-ns #'private access.\n\nVerify and report exactly: clj -M:kondo --lint <changed files>; cljstyle check (say if blocked); focused JVM over\nyin.vm-test, yin.vm.engine-test (if present), yin.vm.ffi-test, yin.vm.semantic-test, yin.vm.semantic-ffi-test,\nyin.vm.parity-test, yin.vm.debruijn-register-effects-test, yin.vm.ucf.remote-test, yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve-test,\nyin.vm.ffi.remote-serve.responder-test, any new test ns, dao.stream.apply-test; then the FULL clj -M:test and\nbb test:cljs (VM-wide change). Do NOT run bb test:cljd. Known flake: yin.repl.main-test cross-process; report, don't fix.\n\nWrite the report to collab/1790655248000-vm-engineer-ffi-caller-correlation.claude-opus-5-5.report.md and give it as your\nfinal response, beginning exactly with:\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\nCoding-Agent: claude\nSession-ID: 08d36f7d-b33d-404e-adcb-dc04d5b907ef\nReport changed files, exact test outcomes, acceptance a-g -> tests, every existing test you modified and why, design\nchoices where the rulings left latitude, unresolved concerns, and incomplete work.\n## Changes to the ruling (precise)\n\n1. **The required-files list is missing `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc`.** The wait-entry validators enforce `(keyword? (:call-id entry))` for both the ffi-writer and ffi-reader shapes (`debruijn_register_effects.cljc:412` and `:432`). The composite `[caller-token local-park-id]` is a vector and fails both. The slice must extend those validators (and `test/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects_test.cljc`) to the composite shape — e.g. a keyword *or* a plain-data 2-vector whose second element is the local park id. Without this, register-VM FFI waits are refused by the contract tests.\n2. **Decide the supplied-pair default.** Recommendation: when `:call-in`/`:call-out` are supplied without `:call-out-cursor`, refuse — extend the half-a-pair check (`vm.cljc:2012-2016`). An implicit `:oldest` mint on a shared exported medium is not merely slow but loss-prone: the router scans retained history, and a mid-scan eviction raises terminal gap-loss for waiters whose own answers may still be ahead — a likelihood an oldest anchor on a busy shared ring invites and a composition-supplied `:newest` cursor avoids. Softer fallback (owner decision): keep the `:oldest` default and document it as such.\n3. **End/gap distinguishing key** (D above).\n4. **Router dispatch details the ruling should name:** (a) the discriminator must match both entry shapes — the walker nests `:call-id` in `:k` (`ffi.cljc:56-59`) while semantic/stack/register place it at top level (`ffi.cljc:82`, `semantic.cljc:111-115`); (b) waiters are grouped per cursor cell, and lowered retained calls wait on *carried* cells that are not `vm/call-out-cursor-key` (`semantic.cljc:118-128`, `ucf/remote.cljc:622-633`) — \"each response cursor cell\" must explicitly include carried cells; (c) FFI response entries must be excluded from the generic sweep exactly as link entries are (`engine.cljc:1346-1350`); (d) the apply-value interpretation may live in `yin.vm.ffi` with `check-wait-set` dispatching into it (no cycle: `ffi.cljc` requires only `vm`/`telemetry`, so engine→ffi→vm is acyclic), which keeps envelope interpretation out of the engine; either placement conforms.\n5. **Token constraint:** the caller token must satisfy `vm/plain-data?` and the channel codec (string, uuid, or keyword). Add a CLJD assertion that a vector-valued parked key round-trips (ClojureDart vector equality as a map key).\n\n## OWNER decisions\n\n1. Authorization to edit the VM files — now **eight**: the ruling's seven plus `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc` (and its test).\n2. Supplied-pair cursor policy: refuse-without-cursor (recommended) vs documented `:oldest` default.\n3. The deployment choices the ruling already lists (token minting authority, handler/renewal authority, channel adapter, capacity, lease timing) — unchanged; composition inputs, no further ruling needed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
