c:595:   the carried response route (`:response-cursor`,\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:651:                            :response-cursor\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:712:   writes through its carried request reflection's allocated key and\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:713:   stamps the carried response route (`:response-cursor`,\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:717:   reflection. `contexts`, parallel to `pendings`, is each entry's\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/responder.cljc:150:(defn- close-call-out!\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/responder.cljc:154:      (stream/close! out))))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/caller.cljc:7:   without `:call-out-cursor`). Over reflections of a served endpoint\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/caller.cljc:8:   that cursor is a remote answer: the reflection's first `cursor`\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/caller.cljc:14:   `open` attaches both reflections of an apply endpoint and checks the\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/caller.cljc:15:   caller token. `step` asks the call-out reflection once for a\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/caller.cljc:23:   cursor, and the caller token -- for any VM's `create-vm`.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/caller.cljc:64:   unique per tenure (`yin.vm/ffi-caller-id?`). Optional:\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/caller.cljc:70:   when an option is malformed, or naming the reflection that did not\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/caller.cljc:78:      (not (vm/ffi-caller-id? caller-id)) (refused ::caller-id ::malformed)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/caller.cljc:96:  \"Ask the call-out reflection once for a `:dao.stream/newest` cursor.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/caller.cljc:137:  \"The construction options a ready caller hands any VM's `create-vm`:\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/caller.cljc:138:   `:call-in`, `:call-out`, `:call-out-cursor` and `:ffi-caller-id`.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/caller.cljc:145:     :ffi-caller-id (::caller-id caller)}))\nsrc/cljc/yin/